# ── Personal-data firewall ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo ships as a TEMPLATE. As you fill it with your own life, keep the
# private parts out of git until YOU choose otherwise. Uncomment what applies.

# Cross-session agent memory (frequently holds personal facts)
MEMORY.md
memory/

# Generated full-brain snapshot (large, personal — built by /load-brain)
.claude/brain_snapshot.md

# Centralized personal values, if you add a profile layer
/profile/

# Secrets / environment
.env
*.env
**/credentials*
**/*secret*

# Machine-specific settings overrides (local perms/paths)
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS / editor / build cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
node_modules/
.pytest_cache/

# ── Privacy depth (see Orientation_Docs/PRIVACY_DEPTH.md) ─────────────────
# Keep the local depth manifest and your most-private (depth 4–5) material out of git.
DEPTH_INDEX.json
*.depth_manifest.json

# ── Your private content folders ─────────────────────────────────────────
# These ship empty/synthetic. Once you put REAL private content in them and you
# do NOT want it public, uncomment the ones that apply BEFORE committing:
# /Journal_Personal/
# /Health/
# /Personal_Operations/
